Adobe websites (adobeDataLayer)Google Analytics websites (dataLayer)Mobile apps <pre><code>window.adobeDataLayer = window.adobeDataLayer || [];
window.adobeDataLayer.push({
  'event': 'universal_click',
  'universalClickthroughComponent': '&lt;component type&gt;',
  'universalClickthroughLabel': '&lt;label&gt;',
  'universalClickthroughURL': '&lt;destination URL&gt;'
});
</code></pre> <pre><code>window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
window.dataLayer.push({
  'event': 'universal_click',
  'universalClickthroughComponent': '&lt;component type&gt;',
  'universalClickthroughLabel': '&lt;label&gt;',
  'universalClickthroughURL': '&lt;destination URL&gt;'
});
</code></pre> <pre><code>MobileCore.track(action: "universal_click", data: [
    "universalClickthroughComponent": "button",
    "universalClickthroughLabel": "Get in touch",
    "universalClickthroughURL": "https://www.example.com/contact-us"
])
</code></pre> Key What it holds Examples <code>universalClickthroughComponent</code> The type of UI element clicked <code>link</code>, <code>button</code>, <code>banner</code> <code>universalClickthroughLabel</code> The text shown on the element <code>Get in touch</code> <code>universalClickthroughURL</code> The full <code>href</code> of the link <code>https://www.example.com/contact-us</code> <p>Example</p> <pre><code>{
  "event": "universal_click",
  "universalClickthroughComponent": "button",
  "universalClickthroughLabel": "Get in touch",
  "universalClickthroughURL": "https://www.example.com/contact-us"
}
</code></pre> <p>If developers cannot add the push</p> <p>A Launch click rule on <code>a[href]</code> can read the element's text and <code>href</code> itself, with no developer work. It is less reliable (text changes, buttons that are not links) and the component type has to be guessed, so use it only as a stop-gap.</p>

Adobe LaunchGoogle Tag ManagerMobile apps <p>Paste in the <code>&lt;head&gt;</code>, as high as possible:</p> <pre><code>&lt;script&gt;window.adobeDataLayer = window.adobeDataLayer || [];&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;script src="&lt;LAUNCH EMBED URL&gt;" async&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Use the staging embed URL on staging and the production one on the live site. Both come from Launch (Environments &gt; Install). Add the Adobe Client Data Layer extension in the property, so the library handles <code>adobeDataLayer</code>.</p> <p>Paste in the <code>&lt;head&gt;</code>, as high as possible:</p> <pre><code>&lt;!-- Google Tag Manager --&gt;
&lt;script&gt;window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;script&gt;(function(w,d,s,l,i){w[l]=w[l]||[];w[l].push({'gtm.start':
new Date().getTime(),event:'gtm.js'});var f=d.getElementsByTagName(s)[0],
j=d.createElement(s),dl=l!='dataLayer'?'&amp;l='+l:'';j.async=true;j.src=
'https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id='+i+dl;f.parentNode.insertBefore(j,f);
})(window,document,'script','dataLayer','GTM-XXXXXXX');&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;!-- End Google Tag Manager --&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Paste immediately after the opening <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> tag:</p> <pre><code>&lt;!-- Google Tag Manager (noscript) --&gt;
&lt;noscript&gt;&lt;iframe src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/ns.html?id=GTM-XXXXXXX"
height="0" width="0" style="display:none;visibility:hidden"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/noscript&gt;
&lt;!-- End Google Tag Manager (noscript) --&gt;
</code></pre> <p>Replace <code>GTM-XXXXXXX</code> with the container ID. For staging, GTM gives an environment-specific snippet with extra parameters (<code>gtm_auth</code>, <code>gtm_preview</code>). Copy it from Admin &gt; Environments &gt; Get Snippet.</p> <p>The developers add the Adobe Experience Platform Mobile SDK and register the extensions with the app ID from the Launch mobile property, using the development, staging and production environment IDs.</p>

