Adobe websites (adobeDataLayer)Google Analytics websites (dataLayer)Mobile apps <pre><code>window.adobeDataLayer = window.adobeDataLayer || [];
window.adobeDataLayer.push({
  'event': 'form_start',
  'formId': '&lt;CMS form ID&gt;',
  'formType': '&lt;form type&gt;',
  'formName': '&lt;form name&gt;'
});
</code></pre> <p>On <code>form_complete</code>, add the submission ID:</p> <pre><code>window.adobeDataLayer = window.adobeDataLayer || [];
window.adobeDataLayer.push({
  'event': 'form_complete',
  'formId': '&lt;CMS form ID&gt;',
  'formType': '&lt;form type&gt;',
  'formName': '&lt;form name&gt;',
  'submissionId': '&lt;submission ID&gt;'
});
</code></pre> <pre><code>window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
window.dataLayer.push({
  'event': 'form_start',
  'formId': '&lt;CMS form ID&gt;',
  'formType': '&lt;form type&gt;',
  'formName': '&lt;form name&gt;'
});
</code></pre> <p>On <code>form_complete</code>, add the submission ID:</p> <pre><code>window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
window.dataLayer.push({
  'event': 'form_complete',
  'formId': '&lt;CMS form ID&gt;',
  'formType': '&lt;form type&gt;',
  'formName': '&lt;form name&gt;',
  'submissionId': '&lt;submission ID&gt;'
});
</code></pre> <pre><code>MobileCore.track(action: "form_start", data: [
    "formId": "&lt;CMS form ID&gt;", "formType": "&lt;form type&gt;", "formName": "&lt;form name&gt;"
])
</code></pre> <pre><code>MobileCore.trackAction("form_complete", mapOf(
    "formId" to "&lt;CMS form ID&gt;", "formType" to "&lt;form type&gt;",
    "formName" to "&lt;form name&gt;", "submissionId" to "&lt;submission ID&gt;"
))
</code></pre> Key Sent on What it holds Examples <code>formId</code> all four events ID of the form in the CMS or form tool <code>contact-us-01</code> <code>formType</code> all The kind of form. Use the agreed list <code>Contact us</code>, <code>Subscription</code>, <code>Workshop registration</code> <code>formName</code> all The name of the form, or the selected variant <code>General enquiry</code>, <code>Subscription</code> <code>formStep</code> <code>form_step</code>, <code>form_error</code> Step number and name <code>2 - Company details</code> <code>submissionId</code> <code>form_complete</code> Unique ID for this submission, for example the reference returned by the server <code>SUB-20261029-0042</code> <p>Example (<code>form_complete</code>)</p> <pre><code>{
  "event": "form_complete",
  "formId": "contact-us-01",
  "formType": "Contact us",
  "formName": "General enquiry",
  "submissionId": "SUB-20261029-0042"
}
</code></pre> <p>Never send what the visitor typed</p> <p>Send only the keys above. Never send field values, not even an email address, a name or a hash of them. <code>submissionId</code> must be a reference number and must not contain personal data.</p>

Adobe Analytics (AppMeasurement)Adobe Web SDK (XDM)Adobe Mobile SDKGoogle Analytics 4 (GTM) Data element Type Purpose <code>DL - pageName</code> Data Layer Computed State, path <code>pageName</code> Name from the data layer, if developers push it <code>Code - page name</code> Custom code Name from the URL, the default (below) Rule Trigger Actions <code>PLR - Global: Page View</code> Page Bottom (or <code>page_view</code> data layer event for single-page apps) Set Variables: Page Name = <code>%Code - page name%</code>, <code>EVAR_PAGE_NAME</code> = <code>%Code - page name%</code>. Send Beacon, page view <p>Custom code (only if needed), for <code>Code - page name</code>. It prefers the data layer and falls back to the URL:</p> <pre><code>var dl = _satellite.getVar('DL - pageName');
if (dl) return dl;
var path = location.pathname.replace(/\.(html|page|aspx)$/, '')
                            .replace(/\/index$/, '')
                            .replace(/^\/|\/$/g, '');
var parts = path ? path.split('/') : ['home'];
return ['acme'].concat(parts).join(':').toLowerCase();
</code></pre> <p>Same data elements. In the XDM object for the page view, set <code>eventType</code> to <code>web.webpagedetails.pageViews</code>, <code>web.webPageDetails.name</code> to <code>%Code - page name%</code> and <code>web.webPageDetails.pageViews.value</code> to <code>1</code>. In Analytics, <code>web.webPageDetails.name</code> becomes the Page Name. Copy the name to <code>EVAR_PAGE_NAME</code> through the mapping.</p> <p>Developers use screen names in the same format. No processing rule is needed for the Page Name. If a copy in <code>EVAR_PAGE_NAME</code> is needed, add a rule: Page Name exists, set <code>EVAR_PAGE_NAME</code> = Page Name.</p> <p>GA4 sends <code>page_view</code> with the page title and URL automatically. Add the name as an extra parameter:</p> Item Setup Variable <code>DLV - pageName</code>, or a Custom JavaScript variable that builds the name from the URL Google tag settings Add a parameter <code>page_name</code> = that variable GA4 Admin Register <code>page_name</code> as an event-scoped custom dimension

Adobe websites (adobeDataLayer)Google Analytics websites (dataLayer)Mobile apps <pre><code>window.adobeDataLayer = window.adobeDataLayer || [];
window.adobeDataLayer.push({
  'event': 'search_results',
  'searchTerm': '&lt;search term&gt;',
  'searchResultsCount': '&lt;number of results&gt;',
  'searchType': '&lt;where the search started&gt;'
});
</code></pre> <pre><code>window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
window.dataLayer.push({
  'event': 'view_search_results',
  'searchTerm': '&lt;search term&gt;',
  'searchResultsCount': '&lt;number of results&gt;',
  'searchType': '&lt;where the search started&gt;'
});
</code></pre> <pre><code>MobileCore.track(action: "search_results", data: [
    "searchTerm": "home loan", "searchResultsCount": "12", "searchType": "app search"
])
</code></pre> Key What it holds Examples <code>searchTerm</code> What the visitor typed, trimmed <code>home loan</code> <code>searchResultsCount</code> Number of results shown, as a number <code>0</code>, <code>12</code> <code>searchType</code> Where the search started. Use the agreed list <code>header</code>, <code>results page</code>, <code>suggestion</code> <p>Event name differs by platform</p> <p>The Adobe push uses <code>search_results</code>. The Google push uses GA4's recommended name <code>view_search_results</code>. Everything else is the same.</p> <p>Personal data in search boxes</p> <p>People type names and account numbers into search boxes. Ask developers to remove anything that looks like an email address or a long number before the push. The tagging team removes them again in Launch as a safety net.</p>

Adobe Analytics (AppMeasurement)Adobe Web SDK (XDM)Adobe Mobile SDKGoogle Analytics 4 (GTM) Data element Type Path / purpose <code>DL - searchTerm</code> Data Layer Computed State <code>searchTerm</code> (lower case, trimmed) <code>DL - searchResultsCount</code> Data Layer Computed State <code>searchResultsCount</code> <code>DL - searchType</code> Data Layer Computed State <code>searchType</code> <code>Code - search results bucket</code> Custom code Turns the count into <code>0</code>, <code>1-5</code>, <code>6-20</code>, <code>21+</code> (below) Rule Trigger Actions <code>ACDL - Search: Results by "search_results"</code> Data layer event <code>search_results</code> Set Variables: <code>EVAR_SEARCH_TERM</code>, <code>PROP_SEARCH_TERM</code>, <code>EVAR_SEARCH_RESULTS</code> = <code>%Code - search results bucket%</code>, <code>EVAR_SEARCH_TYPE</code>, event <code>EVENT_SEARCH</code>. Send Beacon, custom link, <code>Internal Search</code> <code>ACDL - Search: No results by "search_results"</code> Same trigger. Condition: <code>DL - searchResultsCount</code> equals <code>0</code> Set Variables: event <code>EVENT_SEARCH_NULL</code>. Send Beacon, <code>Internal Search No Results</code> <p>Custom code (only if needed), for the <code>Code - search results bucket</code> data element:</p> <pre><code>var n = parseInt(_satellite.getVar('DL - searchResultsCount'), 10) || 0;
return n === 0 ? '0' : n &lt;= 5 ? '1-5' : n &lt;= 20 ? '6-20' : '21+';
</code></pre> <p>To remove an email address or long number, add this to the term data element's Custom code option, or use a Code data element: <code>term.replace(/\S+@\S+/g, '').replace(/\d{6,}/g, '')</code>.</p> <p>Rule and data elements as in the AppMeasurement tab. XDM object: <code>eventType</code> <code>web.webinteraction.linkClicks</code> (or a custom <code>search.results</code>), search fields in your custom <code>search</code> field group: <code>term</code>, <code>resultsCount</code>, <code>type</code>. Map them to the eVars and prop in the Analytics mapping. Use the same results bucket data element.</p> <p>Processing Rules:</p> Condition Set Action name equals <code>search_results</code> <code>EVENT_SEARCH</code> Action name equals <code>search_results</code> and context data <code>searchResultsCount</code> equals <code>0</code> <code>EVENT_SEARCH_NULL</code> Context data <code>searchTerm</code> exists <code>EVAR_SEARCH_TERM</code> and <code>PROP_SEARCH_TERM</code> Context data <code>searchType</code> exists <code>EVAR_SEARCH_TYPE</code> <p>Ask the developers to send the results bucket (<code>0</code>, <code>1-5</code>, <code>6-20</code>, <code>21+</code>) as <code>searchResultsCount</code>, or add a processing rule that sets <code>EVAR_SEARCH_RESULTS</code> from the number.</p> Item Setup Variables <code>DLV - searchTerm</code>, <code>DLV - searchResultsCount</code>, <code>DLV - searchType</code> Trigger <code>CE - view_search_results</code> Tag <code>GA4 - View Search Results</code>, event <code>view_search_results</code>, parameters <code>search_term</code>, <code>search_results</code>, <code>search_type</code> Second trigger and tag Same trigger plus condition <code>DLV - searchResultsCount</code> equals <code>0</code>; tag <code>GA4 - Search No Results</code>, event <code>search_no_results</code> GA4 Admin Register <code>search_results</code> and <code>search_type</code> as custom dimensions <p>If the site's search uses a URL parameter such as <code>?q=</code>, GA4's enhanced measurement can collect <code>view_search_results</code> automatically. Turn that off when you use the data layer push, to avoid duplicates.</p>

Adobe Analytics (AppMeasurement)Adobe Web SDK (XDM)Adobe Mobile SDKGoogle Analytics 4 (GTM) Data element Type Purpose <code>Code - site section 1</code> to <code>Code - site section 4</code> Custom code Each returns one level from the data layer, or from the page name (below) <p>The page-load rule <code>PLR - Global: Page View</code> gets extra fields in its Set Variables action:</p> Field Value Channel <code>%Code - site section 1%</code> <code>EVAR_SITE_SECTION</code> <code>%Code - site section 1%</code> <code>PROP_SECTION_L2</code> to <code>PROP_SECTION_L4</code> <code>%Code - site section 2%</code> to <code>%Code - site section 4%</code> <p>Custom code (only if needed), one data element per level (change the index, 2 for level 1):</p> <pre><code>var dl = _satellite.getVar('DL - siteSection1');
if (dl) return dl;
return (_satellite.getVar('Code - page name').split(':')[2] || '');  // 2 = level 1, 3 = level 2, 4 = level 3, 5 = level 4
</code></pre> <p>This assumes the page name starts with <code>site:country:</code>.</p> <p>Same data elements. Level 1 goes to <code>web.webPageDetails.siteSection</code>. The other levels go to custom fields in your schema, mapped to the props in the Analytics mapping.</p> <p>Processing Rules: context data <code>siteSection1</code> sets the Channel variable and <code>EVAR_SITE_SECTION</code>. <code>siteSection2</code> to <code>siteSection4</code> set the props.</p> Item Setup Variables <code>DLV - siteSection1</code> to <code>DLV - siteSection4</code>, or custom JavaScript variables that split the page name Google tag settings <code>content_group</code> = level 1. Parameters <code>section_l2</code>, <code>section_l3</code>, <code>section_l4</code> GA4 Admin Register <code>section_l2</code> to <code>section_l4</code> as custom dimensions

